WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.160
Unit twenty-four. Hearing and Noise!

2
00:00:04.119 --> 00:00:07.762
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.812 --> 00:00:10.864
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.914 --> 00:00:14.332
Today we learn about Hearing and Noise. Let's go!

5
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:18.456
Hearing. Say it with me. Hearing!

6
00:00:21.959 --> 00:00:25.325
Noise. Say it with me. Noise!

7
00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:32.581
Headphones. Say it with me. Headphones!

8
00:00:36.111 --> 00:00:39.178
Volume. Say it with me. Volume!

9
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.084
Decibel. Say it with me. Decibel!

10
00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.615
Ringing. Say it with me. Ringing!

11
00:00:56.072 --> 00:00:59.388
Protection. Say it with me. Protection!

12
00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:05.910
Break. Say it with me. Break!

13
00:01:09.404 --> 00:01:18.448
Loud noise can permanently damage hearing. Keep headphones at a safe volume and take a break. Ringing in the ears is a warning sign, so use protection at loud events.

14
00:01:18.498 --> 00:01:21.234
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:22.592 --> 00:01:27.673
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:27.723 --> 00:01:28.873
Headphones!

17
00:01:29.994 --> 00:01:35.149
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:35.199 --> 00:01:36.349
Protection!

19
00:01:37.268 --> 00:01:43.776
Did you know? A common rule is to keep headphone volume below 60% for no more than 60 minutes at a time!

20
00:01:43.826 --> 00:01:45.999
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:47.361 --> 00:01:55.290
Think and answer. How can you protect your hearing when using headphones?

22
00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.490
Great answer!

23
00:01:57.573 --> 00:02:02.433
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:05.099
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

